# Project-wide rules (minimal, high-signal)

This ruleset intentionally keeps only non-obvious, repository-specific requirements.

## Core

- Make the smallest change that fully solves the task.
- Prefer existing patterns in nearby files over introducing new abstractions.
- In `app/`, write JavaScript/JSX (not TypeScript) unless explicitly requested.
- Add and fix JSDoc types on every new or changed export in `app/` — see [jsdoc-types.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/jsdoc-types.mdc).

## Imports and logging

- For imports inside `app/`, use the `#/*` alias instead of deep relative paths.
- Do not include file extensions in imports.
- On the server, use `#/utils/logger.server` for logging; avoid `console.log`.

## Validation

- Before finishing, run at least one relevant validation step for touched code (targeted test, lint, or build command).
- Add new persistent rules only when they fix repeated agent mistakes.
